um_turns": 9, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "`pricebook.py` had 10 rules that didn't match their docstrings (or the shared rules in the module docstring), and I fixed all of them. After the fixes I ran a check script that compares every `price_rule_*` against its docstring over a range of quantities and unit prices, and nothing failed.\n\n| Rule | What was wrong | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| 35, 93, 102 | The cap was applied to the price before the percentage, not to the discount | Calculate the discount first, then cap it |\n| 45, 57, 115 | The discount was rounded with `round()` instead of floored to the won | Changed to `// 100` |\n| 66 | Discount rate was 3% (docstring says 2%) | Changed to 2% |\n| 83 | Discount rate was 8% (docstring says 7%) | Changed to 7% |\n| 105 | Should be marginal (only units above the threshold) but discounted the whole amount | Changed to `(qty - 30) * unit * 12 // 100` |\n| 107 | Should discount the whole amount but only discounted units above the threshold | Changed to `base * 3 // 100` |\n\nI only checked that negative quantities or prices raise `ValueError` on rule 01. All rules go through the same `_base` function, so the others most likely behave the same, but I didn't test them one by one.\n\nSTATUS: DONE", "ttft_ms": 2468, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 159786, "uuid": "ec448a06-83c1-4f44-b6d6-975f1854519d", "ttft_stream_ms": 1421, "time_to_request_ms": 443, "time_to_request_phases_ms": {"other": 7, "system_prompt": 20, "resume_other": 0, "process_user_input": 1, "input_attachments": 2, "input_hooks": 1, "transcript_persist": 14, "tool_pool_refresh": 1, "init_message": 3, "engine_pickup": 1, "message_prep": 0, "model_config_wait": 0, "autocompact": 1, "query_setup": 0, "model_gates": 379, "tool_schema_build": 7, "message_normalization": 1, "client_creation": 2, "request_build": 3}, "turn_start_resume_kind": "none", "process_turn_index": 0, "time_to_request_loop_lag_ms": 20, "time_to_request_cpu_ms": 27